1
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,963
Hey.
Hey.

2
00:00:04,003 --> 00:00:06,005
So, what do
you think?

3
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:07,591
New haircut?

4
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:09,009
Necklace?

5
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,719
Dress.

6
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:11,512
Boots?

7
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,514
Boots!

8
00:00:13,555 --> 00:00:16,809
Yes! Now, they're a little
more than I usually spend

9
00:00:16,851 --> 00:00:19,520
on boots, um...
or rent.

10
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:20,771
Oh, my God.

11
00:00:20,813 --> 00:00:22,189
I know.

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,900
I'm going to miss being able
to afford food.

13
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:26,193
I'm sorry.

14
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,736
They just
looked so good.

15
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:29,363
And the saleswoman was
looking at me like

16
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:30,948
"These are way too
expensive for you."

17
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:32,449
She had a point.

18
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,075
( knocking on door )

19
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:36,119
Hi.
Hey.

20
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,538
Oh, my God.

21
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:38,330
Oh, Monica.

22
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:41,124
Those boots
are amazing!

23
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,335
They're mine!

24
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:46,005
Yeah, well, too bad we're going
to have to return them.

25
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:47,088
Return them?! Shh!

26
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,716
They're going
to hear you!

27
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,385
Honey, I'm not returning them,
okay?

28
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,928
I mean,
I know they cost a lot

29
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:55,222
but I'm going to wear them
all the time-- you'll see.

30
00:00:55,263 --> 00:00:56,807
And besides,
I love the compliments.

31
00:00:56,849 --> 00:00:59,810
I mean, have you ever had
something that was so beautiful

32
00:00:59,852 --> 00:01:01,562
that everyone wants it?

33
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:02,646
I have you.

34
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:04,732
Nice try.
I'm keeping the boots.

35
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:13,615
Anyway, look...

36
00:01:13,657 --> 00:01:16,493
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

37
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:19,079
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

38
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,041
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

39
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:25,920
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

40
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:28,380
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

41
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,592
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

42
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:34,845
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

43
00:01:34,887 --> 00:01:38,557
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

44
00:01:45,898 --> 00:01:48,901
That's right,
I love you...

45
00:01:48,943 --> 00:01:52,571
and I'm going
to play with you
all the time.

46
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:55,866
How can you let him
talk to your crotch like that?

47
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:01,121
He's talking
to the baby.

48
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:03,331
Oh, okay!

49
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:06,585
Okay, 'cause when he said

50
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:08,127
"I can't wait to hear
your first words."

51
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:09,671
I thought, "There's a trick."

52
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:14,301
Okay... well, I got to go,
you guys.

53
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,719
I'll see you later.

54
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:16,804
Okay.
Okay. Bye.

55
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,305
Bye.

56
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,890
Oh, hey, Rach,
listen-- hi.

57
00:02:19,932 --> 00:02:20,975
Hi.

58
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:22,101
Um, can you do
me a favor?

59
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,435
I was talking
to my sister

60
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:24,645
and she knows you
work at Ralph Lauren--

61
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,814
Forget it-- no way--
I am not sending

62
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:30,233
any more Ralph Lauren clothes
to prison; it is a waste.

63
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,652
No, no, no, no.
Not her, not her.

64
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,861
My youngest
sister, Deena--

65
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:34,488
she's really
interested in fashion

66
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,406
and she wants to talk
to someone successful

67
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:37,950
to, you know, give
her some advice.

68
00:02:37,992 --> 00:02:39,952
I guess she could talk
to one of my supervisors.

69
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:42,162
No, no, no, she wants
to talk to you.

70
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:43,998
Really?

71
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:45,165
Oh, my God!

72
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,668
I'm successful.

73
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,003
So, will you
meet with her?

74
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:50,838
Yes, I'd love to.
Have her come by
the office.

75
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,798
Great. Thanks.
You're going to
love her so much.

76
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:55,676
And, oh, she's the
smartest of all the
Tribbiani children.

77
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,136
Yeah, you know
the SATs?

78
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:58,137
Yeah.

79
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,346
She took them.

80
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:04,183
Hey, Ross, doesn't Ben go
to Smithfield Day School?

81
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:05,519
Yeah, why?

82
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,437
Sting has a son
that goes there, too.

83
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:08,897
Yeah, I know.
He's in Ben's class.

84
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,692
You knew this
and you never said anything?

85
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:15,029
With all the stupid
dinosaur stuff you tell us?

86
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:17,698
Fine. No more dinosaur stuff.

87
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,282
Can I talk
about fossils?

88
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,909
( groans )

89
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:28,207
"Sting's son,
seven years old."

90
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:29,459
And there's a picture.

91
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:30,961
What are you reading

92
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:33,380
The Kidnapper's Guide
to Manhattan Private Schools?

93
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,841
No, it's New York
magazine.

94
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:38,259
It's an article about
the best schools in
the city.

95
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:40,554
So, how well do
you know Sting?

96
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,514
I actually haven't
even met him.

97
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:43,807
Uh-huh. Yeah.
That's too bad.

98
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:46,143
I really want to go to
his concert Friday night

99
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:47,561
but it's totally
sold out.

100
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:48,478
I know!

101
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,313
Why don't you
meet him...

102
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,690
and get tickets!

103
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:54,568
If you get two,
I'll take you.

104
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,319
Well, actually,
I'm picking Ben up tomorrow.

105
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:57,362
Maybe he'll be there.

106
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:58,530
There you go!

107
00:03:58,572 --> 00:03:59,948
Oh, you're so lucky.

108
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:02,076
You might actually get
to meet Sting tomorrow.

109
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:04,285
That's why
you have kids.

110
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:12,878
Hey, guys.
Hey.

111
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,713
Hi, Monica.
Hi.

112
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:16,757
Hi, boots.

113
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:19,384
See, Chandler,
I'm getting a lot of use

114
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:20,594
out of them already.

115
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:22,262
They're very practical.

116
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:24,014
See, you can wear them
with dresses

117
00:04:24,056 --> 00:04:25,515
with skirts, with pants...

118
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,350
You can wear them with shorts
on the street corner

119
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:30,187
and earn the money
to pay for them.

120
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:33,023
Wow. They're beautiful.

121
00:04:33,065 --> 00:04:35,275
They hurt so much!

122
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:36,484
What?!

123
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:38,486
The guy who made these

124
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:41,115
hates feet and wants
to see them die.

125
00:04:41,156 --> 00:04:42,657
Well, give them to me.

126
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:44,659
I haven't felt my feet
in years.

127
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,327
I can't. I spent so
much money on them

128
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,789
and I told Chandler
that I wear them
all the time.

129
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,373
I can't just
give them away.

130
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,500
Well, then get your money back
and return them.

131
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,877
I can do that, either.

132
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,796
The soles are already
a little scuffed up

133
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:58,090
and the insides are filled
with my blood.

134
00:04:58,132 --> 00:04:59,340
Oh.

135
00:05:00,259 --> 00:05:01,635
Hi.
Hey.

136
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:03,678
Hey, I just picked up Ben
from school.

137
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,972
Oh.

138
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:07,849
I don't think you did
a very thorough job.

139
00:05:08,934 --> 00:05:10,560
I dropped him off
at Carol's.

140
00:05:10,602 --> 00:05:12,353
Anyway, it turns out

141
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,273
I'm not going to get
those tickets, though.

142
00:05:14,313 --> 00:05:16,150
Oh, no! Why not?

143
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:19,945
Well, it turns out Ben and
Sting's son do not get along.

144
00:05:19,987 --> 00:05:20,654
How come?

145
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,489
Apparently, Sting's son

146
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,158
made fun of the fact

147
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,534
that Ben's moms are "lesbinems."

148
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:28,787
Wait, but, Ross, if
they don't get along

149
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:30,998
then you should
smooth things over.

150
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,332
Make them be friends.

151
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:35,002
Phoebe, you can't force kids
to be friends.

152
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,253
Sure you can.

153
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:38,421
Give them some blocks.
Put them in a playpen.

154
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:41,049
Playpen?! Ben's seven.

155
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:42,509
Your kid is seven?!

156
00:05:43,802 --> 00:05:46,554
He's really small.

157
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,599
Please, please
get the tickets.

158
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,892
I'm sorry, Pheebs.

159
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:51,977
I just can't do it.

160
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:53,020
Yes, you can.

161
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,813
Sting says so himself.

162
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,231
What?

163
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:59,776
( to tune of "Roxanne" ):
♪ Ross can! ♪

164
00:05:59,818 --> 00:06:02,529
Look, Phe-- I'm sorry,
it's just that--

165
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:06,116
♪ Ross can! ♪

166
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:08,660
Phoebe, I...

167
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:10,662
♪ Ross can, get me
the tickets! ♪

168
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:14,415
♪ Ross can get me the tickets! ♪

169
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:21,340
Here she is--

170
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:23,424
future fashion superstar.

171
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:24,634
Oh, Joey, I'm hardly--

172
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:26,928
My little sister Deena!

173
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:29,181
Right. Hi, Deena.

174
00:06:29,223 --> 00:06:30,265
Nice to meet you.
Hi.

175
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:31,599
Thanks so much
for meeting with me.

176
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:33,227
Joey's told me
so much about you.

177
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:35,020
This is so
exciting for her.

178
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:37,647
Well, I'll let you
two fash... ists

179
00:06:37,689 --> 00:06:39,482
get down to business.

180
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,068
All right...
okay...

181
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:43,070
Okay.

182
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:44,403
All right, Deena.

183
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:47,406
Well, let's talk about
the different areas of fashion

184
00:06:47,448 --> 00:06:49,408
that you could
get involved in.

185
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:51,912
Let's see, there's design--

186
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,039
but you may need a whole
other degree for that--

187
00:06:54,081 --> 00:06:56,124
uh, there's sales,
which is great

188
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:57,625
because you get to travel...

189
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:58,919
I don't care about fashion.

190
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,004
I'm pregnant,
and I know you are, too

191
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:02,756
so you got to help me.

192
00:07:05,217 --> 00:07:07,219
And there's marketing.

193
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:17,645
Oh, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow,
ow, ow!

194
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:22,859
Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh!

195
00:07:22,901 --> 00:07:24,652
Okay.

196
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:29,532
( yelping in pain )

197
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:31,118
What's wrong?

198
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:33,287
Oh, nothing, I just...
I just was yawning.

199
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:36,331
( yelping yawn )

200
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:38,457
Oh, don't forget, my office
holiday party is tonight.

201
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:41,002
Honey, we don't really have to
go to this thing tonight, do we?

202
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,964
Now, sweetie, I know that
you don't like my office parties

203
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:45,924
but you could wear
your new boots.

204
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:51,138
See, every cloud
has a supple leather lining.

205
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:54,891
I don't think that I want
to wear the boots tonight.

206
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:56,017
Why not?

207
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,436
Well, you know,
I'm just worried

208
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:58,603
that your bosses
will see them

209
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:00,063
and think they pay you
too much money.

210
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:04,234
Or your assistant will see them
and want a raise.

211
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:07,821
Do you think I work at some kind
of boot-pricing company?

212
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:10,698
Well, anyway, I've picked out
this outfit that I want to wear

213
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,491
and the boots don't really
go with it.

214
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,328
You said that you
paid all that money

215
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:17,538
because those boots
go with skirts,
dresses and pants.

216
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,458
Fine. And if you want me
to wear the boots

217
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:20,667
I'll wear the boots.

218
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:22,002
In fact, I'll go into
my room right now

219
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,503
and, you know,
try the outfit on.

220
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,005
Okay.

221
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:27,841
Ooh-wee!

222
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:29,343
( giggling )

223
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:31,345
Christmas party
in my boots!

224
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:33,680
( pained laughter )

225
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:38,852
I can't go in there.

226
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,437
I can't tell him.

227
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:42,022
Honey, it's going
to be okay.

228
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:44,691
He has been incredibly
supportive of me.

229
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:46,734
And if he gets
a little upset

230
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:49,488
that's what
the meatball sub is for.

231
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:51,114
Thank you.

232
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,368
Hey!

233
00:08:54,409 --> 00:08:56,911
It's my fashion girls!

234
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,873
What's wrong?

235
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,375
Honey, why don't
you sit down?

236
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:03,877
Deena has something that
she wants to tell you.

237
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:07,381
Oh. What... what's going on?

238
00:09:07,422 --> 00:09:09,757
Is it Mom? Is she sick?

239
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,718
Is it Dad's heart?

240
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,761
Is that a sandwich?

241
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:17,640
Joe, Mom and Dad
are fine.

242
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:19,100
Is that a sandwich?!

243
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:25,106
Joey, there's something
that you should know.

244
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:26,983
Deena?

245
00:09:28,151 --> 00:09:29,944
I'm pregnant.

246
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:32,197
What?!

247
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:33,656
Now-- give him
the sandwich.

248
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:34,741
Give him the
sandwich!

249
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:37,952
Well, obviously,
this is a mistake.

250
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,371
You can't be pregnant

251
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:41,998
because you have to have sex
to get pregnant.

252
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:46,336
Joe, I tried to wait
until I was 25, like you did.

253
00:09:47,546 --> 00:09:49,464
What?! Deena...

254
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:50,257
Oop!

255
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:51,674
Sh--

256
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:54,344
I can't believe this!

257
00:09:54,386 --> 00:09:55,845
You're the good one!

258
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:57,638
You went to college!

259
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,099
Both years!

260
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:03,144
Who did this to you?

261
00:10:03,186 --> 00:10:04,563
Bobby Corso.

262
00:10:04,603 --> 00:10:05,772
But he's a
real nice guy.

263
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,607
I like him a lot.
He's real funny.

264
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:10,026
You got pregnant
for funny?

265
00:10:10,068 --> 00:10:14,822
Deena, if he's funny,
laugh!

266
00:10:17,117 --> 00:10:19,286
I'll be back in a little while.
You stay here.

267
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,370
Why? Where you going?

268
00:10:20,412 --> 00:10:22,414
I can't look at you right now.

269
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:25,417
( heavy sigh )

270
00:10:25,459 --> 00:10:26,626
Wow.

271
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:29,421
I know.

272
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,103
Oh, there you are, Ben.

273
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:45,895
Aunt Phoebe

274
00:10:45,937 --> 00:10:47,147
what are you doing here?

275
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:49,149
Well, I heard
you're having a problem

276
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,858
with one of the boys
in your class

277
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:54,028
and so I thought I would just
come down here

278
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,696
and sit you both down,
have a little talk

279
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,365
and make it all okay.

280
00:10:57,407 --> 00:11:01,495
Now, the boy's name
is Sting's Son.

281
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:04,331
Jack? I hate him.
He's a jerk.

282
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:09,169
Now, Ben, sometimes people may
seem like jerks on the outside

283
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,670
but they have famous fathers.

284
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,006
I have to go.

285
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:15,008
My friend Doug is
waiting for me
over there.

286
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:17,010
Him you're friends with.

287
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:23,975
Excuse me.

288
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,768
Can I help you
with something?

289
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:26,936
Yes. Yes, you can.

290
00:11:26,978 --> 00:11:29,022
I'm looking for
Jack's parents.

291
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,857
Are you with one
of the students?

292
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:32,025
Uh-huh, I'm with Ben.

293
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,776
Are you one of Ben's mothers?

294
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:36,488
I am one of Ben's mothers.

295
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:39,449
I'm a lesbian.

296
00:11:39,491 --> 00:11:42,827
It was difficult
coming out to
my parents.

297
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:45,288
Well, hi.

298
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,456
I'm Jenny Boone.

299
00:11:46,498 --> 00:11:48,124
I'm a new teacher here.

300
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:49,876
I've only met
your partner Carol.

301
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:53,380
Ah, okay, so that would
make me Susan.

302
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:54,589
Right.

303
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:56,216
Are you looking
for Jack's parents

304
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,843
to discuss the problems
he's having with Ben?

305
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:00,094
Yeah, because
I really do think

306
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,013
the parents should
sit down together

307
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:03,431
and have a conversation.

308
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:05,433
Yeah! Let's do that!

309
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:08,853
That... that sounds good.

310
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:10,813
We should sit down
and talk.

311
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:13,400
Just me, my lover Carol
and the Stings.

312
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:16,152
Um, now, how... how will
I get in touch with them?

313
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:17,945
Oh, their number's
on the contact sheet.

314
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,197
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

315
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,449
Could I get
a copy of that

316
00:12:21,491 --> 00:12:23,577
'cause Carol
threw it out.

317
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:24,743
She lost ours.

318
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:26,829
She's such
a scatterbrain.

319
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:29,790
But what a hot
piece of ass.

320
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:37,131
You know, that party
wasn't bad.

321
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:38,132
Yeah.

322
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:40,343
I didn't know
there'd be dancing.

323
00:12:40,385 --> 00:12:41,760
That was a fun surprise.

324
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:42,970
I don't see any cabs.

325
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,723
Maybe we should just walk.

326
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:46,391
No, no, we can't walk.

327
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,602
It's, like, 15 blocks
to the subway.

328
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:49,977
Let's go.

329
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,770
Hey, do you think we can
get the subway right there

330
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:53,648
if we climb down through
that manhole cover?

331
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,942
What's going on?

332
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:58,319
I can't walk, okay?

333
00:12:58,361 --> 00:13:00,530
Okay, these boots
were a huge mistake.

334
00:13:00,572 --> 00:13:01,780
What?

335
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:03,283
Okay, you were right,
all right?

336
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,992
I never should
have bought them.

337
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,953
They're killing me
one toe at a time.

338
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:08,371
So I was right.

339
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:11,583
This is what it
feels like to be right.

340
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:13,876
It's oddly unsettling.

341
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:17,004
How are we going
to get home?

342
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:18,548
Maybe a piggyback ride?

343
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:19,882
Hop on.

344
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,760
Okay, just
give me a second.

345
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,262
Let me just get
my boots off first.

346
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,932
Oh. Oh...

347
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:30,393
Oh... oh, God.

348
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:34,021
Oh... oh... oh...

349
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:37,692
Honey, I know you're
in pain right now

350
00:13:37,734 --> 00:13:39,402
but I'm a little
turned on.

351
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,159
Do you ever worry
that you'll be walking

352
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,454
and your baby will just,
like, slip out?

353
00:13:50,747 --> 00:13:54,626
What college
was that, Deena?

354
00:13:55,669 --> 00:13:57,170
Oh, my God.

355
00:13:57,211 --> 00:13:58,171
Bobby?

356
00:13:58,212 --> 00:14:02,216
Hi, Deena.
Good to see you.

357
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,677
Joey, what are you doing?

358
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,470
Just what needs to be done.

359
00:14:05,512 --> 00:14:10,057
Dearly beloved, we are gathered
here to join...

360
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,476
Joey, this is crazy.

361
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:14,020
Don't interrupt me
when I'm talking to God.

362
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:16,063
Now, where
were we?

363
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:18,483
Oh, right, okay, do you, Deena,
take this man...

364
00:14:18,525 --> 00:14:19,108
No!

365
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:19,858
Oh, you'll take him.

366
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,027
No, I won't.

367
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,487
You don't get
a say in this.

368
00:14:22,529 --> 00:14:23,363
Yes, I do.

369
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,863
I heard "I do."

370
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:26,491
We're halfway there.
Okay, you...

371
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:27,534
All right, Joey

372
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:28,867
that is enough.

373
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:30,829
Listen, as beautiful
and moving as this
ceremony is

374
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,288
this is not legal, okay?

375
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:34,708
They don't have
a marriage license

376
00:14:34,749 --> 00:14:36,459
they don't have
any witnesses

377
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:38,837
and the groom only
has on one shoe.

378
00:14:38,877 --> 00:14:43,216
Yeah, he took
the other one off
and hit me with it.

379
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,718
Well, what am I
supposed to do?

380
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:45,885
You're supposed
to realize

381
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,136
that they are adults

382
00:14:47,178 --> 00:14:48,929
and that they can make
their own decisions.

383
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:49,972
No, they can't.

384
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,725
They were stupid enough

385
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:52,726
to get knocked up.

386
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,435
Hey.

387
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:57,564
Contraceptives are not
always effective.

388
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,565
Right?

389
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:01,942
Yeah... we kind
of didn't use any.

390
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:04,237
Oh, come on, kids,
a little help here.

391
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:13,204
Wow. This place
is incredible.

392
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:14,539
( gasps )

393
00:15:14,581 --> 00:15:17,584
Sting's pen...

394
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,127
that he gave to Phoebe.

395
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:26,259
( gasps )

396
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,053
Come on, secret passageway.

397
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:31,806
Hi.

398
00:15:31,848 --> 00:15:33,474
Hi.

399
00:15:33,516 --> 00:15:34,517
I'm Trudy.

400
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:35,769
You must be Ben's mum.

401
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:38,938
Why else would I be here?

402
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,273
Do sit down.

403
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,232
Uh-huh.

404
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:42,316
I gather Jack and Ben

405
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:43,943
haven't been getting
along lately.

406
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,194
Yeah.

407
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:46,780
I'm sure there are
two sides to this story

408
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:50,867
but all I've heard is that
Ben's a bit of a poo-poo head.

409
00:15:50,909 --> 00:15:52,285
Um, I'm sorry.

410
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:54,120
Won't Jack's father
be joining us?

411
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:56,539
Well, I'm sorry.
Jack's father's
not available.

412
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:58,291
Mm-hmm.

413
00:15:58,332 --> 00:15:59,166
Okay.

414
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,501
Well, then could
we reschedule

415
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:02,462
for say, Friday night,
perhaps at 8:00?

416
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:04,171
Oh, no, I know
that wouldn't work.

417
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,590
My husband's in concert.

418
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:07,216
Concert. Yeah.

419
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:11,304
That just put us
in quite a pickle.

420
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,808
Because you see, I'm very busy
before and after the concert

421
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:16,643
and he's obviously busy during.

422
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:17,811
So, I guess you and I

423
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:20,020
should talk about
Jack and Ben right now.

424
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:23,524
Unless... unless, um...

425
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,986
okay, I would be willing
to go to the concert.

426
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:30,990
All the while, thinking about
the children, of course.

427
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,992
Are you here for tickets?

428
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:34,577
Thank you.

429
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:35,829
Four would be great.

430
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:38,038
Wow. I'm not giving
concert tickets

431
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,792
to someone who'd use
their son like this.

432
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:42,627
Oh, then you're in luck.

433
00:16:42,669 --> 00:16:43,920
Ben's not my son.

434
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:46,172
Look, I've just
pressed a button

435
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:48,090
triggering
a silent alarm.

436
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:50,593
Any minute now the police
will be here.

437
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:52,470
The Police... here?

438
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:56,056
A reunion? Ooh.

439
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:05,733
Okay, ten blocks down,
five to go.

440
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:08,027
Oh, wait.
Stop, stop, stop.

441
00:17:08,068 --> 00:17:10,655
Oh, I'm sorry.
Do you need a break?

442
00:17:12,699 --> 00:17:13,574
My boots in tan.

443
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:14,909
Hey, can you get
a little closer

444
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:15,952
so I can see the price?

445
00:17:15,994 --> 00:17:18,037
I can see it from
right here.

446
00:17:18,078 --> 00:17:20,122
It'll cost you
one husband.

447
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,374
Okay, I'm sorry.

448
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:23,751
I think I can walk
the rest of the way now.

449
00:17:23,793 --> 00:17:25,043
Just give me my boots.

450
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,171
I don't have
your boots.

451
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,840
Well, I don't
have them, either.

452
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:30,257
Where are they?

453
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:33,093
Well, why don't you
check in one of
my saddlebags

454
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:35,095
while I chew on
a bale of hay.

455
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,639
Okay...

456
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:38,725
We've got to go
back and get them.

457
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,018
Honey, are
you seriously

458
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,102
ever going to wear
the boots again?

459
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:44,062
I'm never going
to wear them again.

460
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:48,442
I just didn't get a chance
to say good-bye.

461
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:50,737
You know what?

462
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:53,364
You can say good-bye
to the tan ones.

463
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:54,699
Okay.

464
00:17:54,741 --> 00:17:56,075
All right.

465
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:57,785
Okay.

466
00:17:57,827 --> 00:17:58,786
Bye, boots.

467
00:17:58,828 --> 00:17:59,787
Wait!

468
00:17:59,829 --> 00:18:01,288
Half off?!

469
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:05,209
Joey, just because

470
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,586
they're not
getting married

471
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:09,422
doesn't mean that this
is going to be a disaster.

472
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:10,882
Maybe they have
a plan.

473
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,258
Oh, oh, okay.

474
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:13,676
Okay, let's
hear their plan.

475
00:18:13,718 --> 00:18:16,345
Now, what's the future look like
for Deena and Bobby?

476
00:18:16,387 --> 00:18:22,560
Well... I really have
high hopes for my band.

477
00:18:22,602 --> 00:18:23,895
You were right.

478
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,563
He is funny.

479
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:26,773
RACHEL:
Hey, wait a minute.

480
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,608
I bet when you told
people at first

481
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:31,569
that you wanted to be an actor
they laughed at you.

482
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:32,904
Come on, Bobby

483
00:18:32,946 --> 00:18:34,614
why don't you tell us
a little bit about your band.

484
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:37,366
It's just me
and my pal Rooster.

485
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:40,202
The band's name
is Numb Nuts.

486
00:18:42,747 --> 00:18:44,874
Really?

487
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:48,127
Deena, if you're
having a baby

488
00:18:48,168 --> 00:18:49,545
you should be married.

489
00:18:49,587 --> 00:18:52,172
Even if it is
to Bobby.

490
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,633
Dude, that's not a compliment.

491
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:57,595
You know, Joey, I knew you
wouldn't be supportive.

492
00:18:57,637 --> 00:18:59,305
So, what,
what are you going to do?

493
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:00,473
You going to have
the baby

494
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,808
and raise it
by yourself?

495
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:02,767
Without a husband?

496
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:04,978
You can't be
a single mother alone.

497
00:19:05,019 --> 00:19:07,021
You're going
to ruin your life.

498
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,314
Well, excuse me.

499
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:10,149
Am I ruining my life?

500
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,943
No, no, no,
it's different for you.

501
00:19:11,985 --> 00:19:13,277
You're so strong
and together.

502
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:14,403
You're not
some dumb kid

503
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:16,155
who doesn't know
what she's doing.

504
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,406
Excuse me?

505
00:19:17,448 --> 00:19:20,367
One pregnant woman
at a time, please.

506
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:23,496
I just want you
to be okay.

507
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:25,498
So forcing her
to marry Bobby

508
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,750
is going to make
that happen?

509
00:19:27,792 --> 00:19:29,961
Maybe.

510
00:19:31,462 --> 00:19:35,842
So, what kind
of music does
Numb Nuts...?

511
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:38,011
Aw, forget it.
I can't.

512
00:19:38,052 --> 00:19:39,345
Joey...

513
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,681
I am scared to death about this.

514
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:43,182
But I really think
I can do it.

515
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:44,517
I'm just going
to need some help.

516
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:46,686
And Bobby's going to
be here the whole time.

517
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,604
You bet I am.

518
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:51,357
And to answer your
earlier question

519
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,818
we're straight-up
gangsta rap.

520
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,365
Look, Rachel's told me
how much easier

521
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:01,034
you've made all this
on her.

522
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,618
Why can't you do that for me?

523
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:07,289
Because... because...
because you're my baby sister.

524
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:09,125
And you're my big brother.

525
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:11,169
I mean, you're my
favorite guy

526
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,419
in the whole world.

527
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:15,214
I'm not even scared
to tell Mom and Dad.

528
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:17,257
I was scared of telling you.

529
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:21,721
Well, I'd be scared
of them, but all right.

530
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:24,348
Joey, I can't stand the thought
of having this baby

531
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:27,060
with you mad at me.

532
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:29,227
I want him to have his uncle.

533
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:32,439
Is my baby going to have
his Uncle Joey?

534
00:20:34,525 --> 00:20:37,277
Of course he's going
to have his Uncle Joey.

535
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:40,573
We're going
to be all right.

536
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:42,742
I mean, even
if we're not married

537
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:45,244
this baby is going
to be so loved.

538
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:46,746
And not just by us.

539
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:48,081
That's right.

540
00:20:48,122 --> 00:20:50,249
By his uncle, too.

541
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:53,460
And by you.

542
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:59,425
Okay, Bobby, why don't we
just come over here

543
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:01,886
and let them have
a little moment, okay?

544
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:07,975
Come here.

545
00:21:10,436 --> 00:21:12,980
No, seriously,
what's wrong with you?

546
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:21,655
You're going
to love me so much.
I got Sting tickets!

547
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:24,117
Oh, my God,
I do love you!

548
00:21:24,158 --> 00:21:25,618
How did you do it?

549
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:28,037
Well, let's just say...

550
00:21:28,079 --> 00:21:32,291
♪ Ross can! ♪

551
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:34,085
Where are the seats?

552
00:21:34,127 --> 00:21:35,211
Middle balcony.

553
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:36,796
Okay, would you say
that that's more

554
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,464
than 50 yards
away from Sting

555
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:40,674
his wife or a member
of his family?

556
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:42,009
Yeah.

557
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:44,929
Then that's not
breaking the law. I'm there!

558
00:21:44,971 --> 00:21:48,766
